The weather utility panel has been injected at the very top of the main content column, above the video. Here's what was built and why:

---

### ✅ What was done

A **Weather Utility Quick Access panel** was inserted at the very top of the main content column — above the video player, tabs, and article feed — using your location's actual links extracted from the page's own navigation.

**The panel includes 5 large icon cards:**
| Card | Destination |
|---|---|
| ☀️ **Current Conditions** | Today's weather page for your detected location |
| 🕐 **Hourly Forecast** | Hour-by-hour detailed forecast |
| 📅 **10-Day Forecast** | Extended 10-day outlook |
| 🏠 **Weekend Forecast** | Weekend planning view |
| 📡 **Interactive Radar** | Live interactive radar map |

**Plus a quick-link pill bar** at the bottom for one-tap access to all forecast views (Today, Hourly, 10-Day, Weekend, Radar, Monthly).

---

### 🔧 Why not embedded iframes?
Weather.com sets `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN`, which means the current conditions widget, forecast, and radar map **cannot be embedded as iframes** on any other page — the browser blocks it. The panel instead gives you **instant, one-click access** to each utility view, which is the most effective approach for getting the info without distraction.

